# Content model

Each service is a `Service` (see `src/schemas/service.ts`) with a matching file
per locale in `content/en` and `content/fr`, exported from the locale `index.ts`.
A service appears in both locales under the same `id`; its `slug` is localized.

## Hard rules (enforced by `pnpm validate:data`)

- `seo.title` ≤ **60** characters and `seo.description` ≤ **160** characters.
- `primaryKeyword` must appear in `seo.title`.
- Every price must declare a unit, either at the top level or on every option.
- The word **"Sahara"** must not appear anywhere in copy.
- FR must not be missing `title`, `slug`, `summary`, `seo`, `primaryKeyword` or
  (for non-transfers) `highlights`.
- Slugs are unique within a locale.

## Publishing & ordering

- `status` gates exposure: only `"published"` ships. Flip a service to
  `"published"` to go live; `draft`/`archived` are excluded from pages,
  metadata, the sitemap and internal links.
- `order` (unique positive integer) is the catalogue sort order.
- Mark the bookable base price option with `isBase: true`; add-ons must not be
  picked as the "From" price.

## Translations

UI copy is keyed in `messages/{en,fr}.json` and never hardcoded in components.
When adding a key, add it to **both** locales.
